Infinite Tappestry. Do away with it entirely, but Botches still have bad consequences causing the magick to misfire or twist in dangerous ways. <br /> <br /> Similarly, DA: Mage system does away with Paradox but retains Backlash. You could adapt that.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Paradox suggest that there are laws to reality that are more or less universal/expected, but magick can break. In Realms a wizard defines the rules, in most of the Umbra Spirits define this, and in Earth it's defined by the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Paradox it's a tool made to represent that magick can break reality, but the reality will strike back at the mage for it. You should decide if you want to have this narrative element in that verse, and how much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}